## AI Code Review

This project has a C++ review skill. When using an AI coding assistant:

### Triggering Review

Just ask your AI:
```
review src/main.cpp
```

The skill will automatically:
1. Check for `compile_commands.json` (tool-first)
2. Run clang-tidy if available
3. Review code by priority: UB → Ownership → RAII → Concurrency → Error → API → Performance → Style

### Project Config

Edit `CONSTITUTION.md` to change:
- C++ standard (currently {{ std }})
- Exception policy (currently {{ 'enabled' if exceptions else 'disabled' }})
- Build system (currently {{ build }})

### What Gets Caught

The skill focuses on high-impact mistakes:
- 🔴 Undefined behavior, memory corruption, data races
- 🟠 Lifetime bugs, resource leaks, dangling references
- 🟡 Logic errors, wrong API usage
- 🔵 Modernization opportunities
- ⚪ Style issues (lowest priority)

### File Structure

```
{{ project_name }}/
├── CONSTITUTION.md              # Project config (edit this)
├── AGENTS.md                    # AI entry point
├── references/                  # Detailed C++ rules (loaded on demand)
├── config/                      # clang-tidy profiles
├── GOTCHAS.md                   # Known AI failure patterns
└── scripts/validate.sh          # Project validation
```
